.Dd October 1, 2026
.Dt QCOM_TLMM_ACPI 4 aarch64
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qcom_tlmm_acpi
.Nd "Qualcomm TLMM GPIO controller driver for ACPI systems"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To compile this driver into the kernel,
place the following lines in your
kernel configuration file:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "device gpio"
.Cd "device qcom_tlmm_acpi"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides a
.Xr gpiobus 4
for the general purpose I/O pins of the top level mode multiplexer
(TLMM) of a Qualcomm Snapdragon system-on-chip that boots with ACPI.
It takes the pins as the firmware leaves them, each already in the
function and with the pull its board needs.
Pins in a function other than GPIO can be read but not changed;
the driver never changes a pin's function.
.Pp
The DSDT of these machines lists GPIO consumers from Qualcomm's
reference design, which a board may not share.
The ACPI GPIO bus applies every listed pin's configuration when it
attaches; the
.Nm
driver ignores that, and takes configuration only from the drivers and
programs using a pin afterwards.
Pins the secure world owns, whose registers fault when touched, are not
offered.
.Pp
The
.Xr sdhci 4
driver for the SoCs' SD controllers uses
.Nm
for card detection.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver attaches to ACPI devices with hardware ID
.Qq QCOM060C
on the systems-on-chip it knows, which the DSDT's
.Va \e_SB.SOID
identifies:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Qualcomm Snapdragon 8cx Gen 3 (SC8280XP), 228 pins
.El
.Pp
It has been tested on the Radxa Dragon Q8B.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gpio 3 ,
.Xr gpio 4 ,
.Xr gpiobus 4 ,
.Xr sdhci 4 ,
.Xr gpioctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
driver and this manual page were written by
.An James Kane .
.Sh BUGS
Pin interrupts are not supported, so ACPI GPIO events and
.Qq GpioInt
resources do not work.
